window.ATLAS_PAGES=[{"id":"blackshire-location","region":"Blackshire","title":"Blackshire","body":"Place :Blackshire\nThis land is full of lycanthropes (Werewolves) and elementals, on one side, and Dragons just over the mountains.\nBlackshire\nDarkmoor City Map\nLair of the Wolf\nTemple of the Snake\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":[],"sourcePath":"Blackshire/location.html"},{"id":"blackshire-blackshire","region":"Blackshire","title":"Darkmoor City Map","body":"Blackshire : Darkmoor City Map\nBlackshire\n1 +50 Luck Temporarily\n2 The Howling Moon (Inn)\n3 Blackshire Coach and Buggy\n4 Light Guild Membership (1,000 gold)\n5 Dark Magic Expert (2,000 Gold)\n6 Armor: Mail and Greaves\n7 Outland Trading Post\n8 Wolf's Den\n9 Bank\n10 +50 Spell points\n11 Twillens House\nQuest to place the Statues.\n12 NPC: +2 to all weapons, takes 3% gold\n13 NPC: +10% gold, takes 5% gold\n14 Ty's Trinkets\nSmugglers Guild (upstairs)\n15 Smuggler's Guld Membership (50 gold)\n16 Weapons: Stout Heart Staff and Spear\n17 Maria Trepan\nQuest to destroy the Werewolf Alter\n18\nAdept Guild of Light (1,000 skill)\n19\nAdept Guild of Dark (1,000 skill)\n20 Dragon Tower\nQuest to reset the towers\n21 Master Shield Defense (10 Skill, 5,000 gold)\n22 Master Sword (8 Skill, Cavelier)\n23 Master Mace (8 skill, 40 might, 5,000 gold)\n24 Blackshire Temple\n25 +30 Magic Resistance temporary (will stone you)\n26 Joanne Cravitz\nQuest to rescue Emmanuel from the Temple of the Snake .\n27 +5 Magic resistance permanent (will stone you)\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["Blackshire/Blackshire.gif"],"sourcePath":"Blackshire/Blackshire.html"},{"id":"blackshire-blackshire0","region":"Blackshire","title":"Surrounding area","body":"Blackshire : Surrounding area\n1. Shrine of Magic\n2. Darkmoor\n3. Circus (April, and December?)\n4. Lair of the Wolf [ Map ]\n5. Temple of the Snake [ Map ]\n6. Temple of Baa\n7. Obelisk\n8. The Oasis (Inn)\n9. Lord Kilburn's Shield Quest Item\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["Blackshire/Blackshire0.jpg"],"sourcePath":"Blackshire/Blackshire0.html"},{"id":"blackshire-temple-of-the-snake","region":"Blackshire","title":"Temple of the Snake","body":"Blackshire : Temple of the Snake\nTemple of the Snake\n1. Entrance\n2. A golden dragon, there is a switch down here to let you across to the other hallway.\n3. Emmauel for the Rescue Emmanuel quest is in the cage.\n4. Q see below.\nPlenty of chance to get stoned in here, Medusas and Gorgons are everywhere. It is a small dungeon though. The Golden dragon does not appear to have any blatant weaknesses.\nQ is one healthy dude, even if he does not look like it. He has better than 5,000 hit points, and can cast finder of death until he is dead. Luckily, he is not very accurate with it, I never had it hit me. He does have the Horn of Ros (It allows you to see actual HP of any monster.) The two chests in the room also contain great stuff, one is full of wands, and the other books.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["Blackshire/Temple-of-the-Snake.gif"],"sourcePath":"Blackshire/Temple-of-the-Snake.html"},{"id":"blackshire-lair-of-the-wolf","region":"Blackshire","title":"The Lair of the Wolf","body":"Blackshire : The Lair of the Wolf\nThe Lair of the Wolf\n1. Entrance\n2. Ghost of Balthasar, he asks you to find the Pearl of Putrescence\n3. The Pearl of Purity\nis here walk all the way to the back of the room.\n4. The stairs seem to trigger a transport to the other.\n5. The stairs seem to trigger a transport to the other.\nThere are three types of enemis here, all the forms for Ooze, Swordmen, and Werewolves. It only get's had when you are swarmend by the Greater Werewolves, they can be tough.\nWhen you find the Werewolf Leader, you can kill him and get the Pearl of Putrescence\n.\nit also appeard that certian doors, or points are triggers to regenerate monsters, I don't know how many times I had to clear the same hallway.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["Blackshire/Lair-of-the-Wolf.gif"],"sourcePath":"Blackshire/Lair-of-the-Wolf.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-location","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"Bootleg Bay","body":"Place : Bootleg Bay\nA place with many islands and home of the canibales.\n 1    Bootleg Bay [City Map]\n 2 North Town [City Map]\n 3 Temple of the Tsantsa\n 4 Temple of the Sun [Map]\n 5 Temple of the Fist [Map]\n 6 Hall of the Fire Lord [Map]\n 7 Shrine of Might [Shrine List] pray here in January\n 8 Pedestal\n 9 Fountain [+2 permanent intelligent, if under 15]\n 10 Temple of Baa (healing, donation)\n 11 Fountain [+2 permanent personality, if under 15]\n 12 Fountain of Magic [+20 SP restoration]\n 13 Circus location in December\n 14 Obelisk #11","images":["BootlegBay/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/location.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-city","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"City Map","body":"Bootleg Bay : City Map\n 1    Training (up to level 22)\n 2 Fountain of Magic (+20 SP restoration) [Quest]\n 3 House of Healing\n 4 House with nothing of importance\n 5 Winston Schezar who will give you the Destroy Crystal Quest\n 6 Fountain: +20 Migth boost\n 7 Tavern, fill up for 10 days\n 8 Wapons: Hammer and Tongs\n 9 Expert: Chain Armor Training\n 10 Expert: Perception\n 11 General Store: The Little Magic Shop\n 12 Armor: Abraham's Metalworks\n 13 House with a NPC who will give you +10% gold and takes 5% gold\n 14 House with nothing of importance","images":["BootlegBay/city.gif"],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/city.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-hall-of-the-fire-lord","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"Hall of the Fire Lord","body":"Bootleg Bay : Hall of the Fire Lord\nAncient runes above the entrance attempt to scare away the casual\nvisitor. Fresh goblin tracks lead into and out of the doorway.\nNote: The quest is broken in the original game, the latest patch however fixes\nthis issue. You can earn virtually infinite experience from the quest.\nClick here to learn how the bug works.\nI recommend not to read it, or it will spoil the game fun.\n 1    You start here, the Fire Lord is in this room, talk to him to get a quest.\n 2 This is a huge room, lots of nice fighting in here.\n 3 After falling down a few floors you will be in room 3,\nhere you can kill the \"pharaoph\" look-a-like which should give you a small taste for what\nis to come later on in the game.\nThe complete the quest the fastest way, talk to the Fire Lord in the\nroom you start at. Grab the Amber in the chest nearby and then walk to\nthe East and you will land on top of of a stone block.\nTurn North West and jump into the tunnel, nuke some enemies\nand unward the rigth most door with one of your ambers.\nWith another amber touch one of the stone faces and you will be\nteleported back to the entry hall. Jump down the east floor\nagain and this time jump into the South East tunnel, follow down the\nslope and jump into the hole of the first room. Walk some more and\nfall down one more floor and now head through the North East door.\nYou will encounter a warted door, unward it using one of ambers and\nthe quest is completed. Touch one of the stone faces and talk\nto the Fire Lord. I do not remember if there is a 3rd warted door,\nif so you have to find it before you can unwart the last warted door.","images":["BootlegBay/hall-of-the-fire-lord-pic.jpg","BootlegBay/hall-of-the-fire-lord-shot.jpg","BootlegBay/hall-of-the-fire-lord.gif"],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/hall-of-the-fire-lord.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-bug","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"Hall of the Fire Lord BUG!","body":"Bootleg Bay : Hall of the Fire Lord BUG!\nThe Quest offered by the Fire Lord has a pretty nasty bug. Please do not\nread the following, unless you like to spoil the fun of the game.","images":[],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/bug.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-temple-of-the-fist","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"Temple of the Fist","body":"Bootleg Bay : Temple of the Fist\nThis large but simple structure has become the center of\nworship for a small religious group called the Order of the Fist.\n 1    Secret Switch, most likely makes the Crystal show up.\n 2 Skull Pile, will temporarily remove some Might points.\n 3 Room with the Crystal, destroy it to complete the quest. [Destroy Crystal Quest] .\nx - marks a spot where you can find a treasure chest or the likes","images":["BootlegBay/temple-of-the-fist-pic.jpg","BootlegBay/temple-of-the-fist-shot.jpg","BootlegBay/temple-of-the-fist.gif"],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/temple-of-the-fist.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-temple-of-the-sun","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"Temple of the Sun","body":"Bootleg Bay : Temple of the Sun\nThis forgotten shrine of the Church of the Sun still stands.\nFor all of its ti me in the humid jungle, the temple remaings\nin surprisingly good condition.\n 1    Minotaur King, 500-700 HP\nSacred Chalice (quest item) can be found in one of the chests.\nx - marks a spot where you can find a treasure chest or the likes, in this\ndungeon you will find hidden Sun Ray spell scrolls. Very Powerful!","images":["BootlegBay/temple-of-the-sun-pic.jpg","BootlegBay/temple-of-the-sun-shot.jpg","BootlegBay/temple-of-the-sun.gif"],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/temple-of-the-sun.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-temple-of-tsantsa","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"Temple of Tsantsa","body":"Bootleg Bay : Temple of Tsantsa\nThe smells of death and decay seem to fill the air near this structure.\nThe temple's original purpose has long since been forgotten by\nthe new worshippers.\n 1    Sherrell Ivanareh [Rescue Sherell Quest]\n 2 Cell Key\n 3 Switch, reveals switch at 4\n 4 Switch, reveals switch at 5\n 5 Switch, Opens the large doors to the central room.\nx - marks a spot where you can find a treasure chest or the likes","images":["BootlegBay/temple-of-tsantsa-pic.jpg","BootlegBay/temple-of-tsantsa-shot.jpg","BootlegBay/temple-of-tsantsa.gif"],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/temple-of-tsantsa.html"},{"id":"bootlegbay-city2","region":"Bootleg Bay","title":"Town City Map","body":"Bootleg Bay : Town City Map\n 1    Tavern, fills for 14 days.\n 2 Poison Fountain\n 3 Temple of Tsantsa [Map]\n 4 NPC gives +2 spell skills and takes 5% gold\n 5 NPC gives +1 reputation bonus and takes 10% gold\n 6 NPC gives +2 to armor and weapon skills and takes 6% gold\n 7 Boat Docks: Sails to Main Island on Mondays and Wednesdays","images":["BootlegBay/city2.gif"],"sourcePath":"BootlegBay/city2.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-location","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Castle Ironfist","body":"Place : Castle Ironfist\nCastel Ironfist has many dungeons to explore and more advanced skills can be\nlearned and enhanced to expert level.\n 1    Castle Ironfist [City Map]\n 2 Small Town [City Map]\n 3 Snergle's Caverns [Map]\n 4 Shadow Guild Hideout [Map]\n 5 Temple of Baa [Map]\n 6 Corlagon's Estate [Map]\n 7 Dragoons' Caverns [Map]\n 8 Tavern: The Will o' Wisp (fills to 10)\n 9 The Seer\n 10 Sword in stone (migth 35+?)\n 11 Shrine of Electricity [Shrine List] pray here in September\n 12 Docks: Zephyr, [Travel Schedule]\n 13 Obelisk #?, teleport to castle, fountain +10 HP, enemies respan\n 14 Temple Baa, healing and donation\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/location.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-castle-ironfist","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Castle Ironfist","body":"Castle Ironfist : Castle Ironfist\n 1  Master of Spirit Magic, Spirit Guild Membership\n 2  Expert Body Building\n 3  King's Temple (healing, donation)\n 4  General Store: Eye of Newt\n 5  Initiate Guild of Mind\n 6  Initiate Guild of Spirit\n 7  Initiate Guild of Body\n 8  Body Guild Membership\n 9  Expert Learning Training\n 10  King's Library\n 11  Expert Diplomacy\n 12  Nicolai Ironfist (council member): Quest to Circus\nWilbur Humphrey: Paladin->Cursader (rescue Damsel in Distress)\n 13  +10 Speed (temporarily))\n 14  +10 Accuracy (temporarily)\n 15  Teleport to and from Obelisk\n 16  Iron Defense\n 17  Expert Disarm Training\n 18  Expert Identification\n 19  Expert Axe Training (West side)\nRoyal Gymnasium (Training, East Side)\n 20  Fine Blades\n 21  Expert Swordmanship\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/castle-ironfist.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/castle-ironfist.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-corlagons-estate","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Corlagon's\nEstate","body":"Castle Ironfist : Corlagon's\nEstate\nOnce the residence of Archmage Terrax, Corlagon received the Estate\nfrom Archibald for his services during the Succession Wars.\n 1    Power Lich enemy, protects chest with the Crystal of Terrax of the [Arch Mages Quest] .\n 2 Locked door, open with switch at 4\n 3 Secret door, only opens from the back of the picture\n 4 Switch, open door at 2\n 5 Switch, opens partial wall at 6\n 6 Switch, open door to room 1\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/corlagons-estate-pic.jpg","CastleIronfist/corlagons-estate-shot.jpg","CastleIronfist/corlagons-estate.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/corlagons-estate.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-dragoons-caverns","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Dragoons' Caverns","body":"Castle Ironfist : Dragoons' Caverns\nThe original name of these caverns has been lost in time. Now,\nit is named for the group of bandits that base their operations\nfrom it.\n 1    Six chests (from left to right). 1:teleport, 2:treasure (contains quest item), 3:teleport, 4:teleport, 5:teleport, 6:teleport\n 2 Stone face gives you +10 to luck for the character who touches it.\n 3 Switch in stone table\n 4 Switch in stone table\n 5 Switch in stone table\n 6 Locked Door, opened by switch #5\n 7 Secret Door, opened by touching the wall. Contains 2 switches\n 8 Secret Room, oppend by using switch from room #4. Here you will find the Orders from the Shadow Guild message scrool which is needed for the [Shadow Guild Proof Quest] . Note that the chest contains a secret. Open it the first time and clean it out. The 2nd time you open it, a new treasure will be inside.\nNote that this level has quite a few Ooze monster that are imune to physical damage.\nOnly go down into the water tunnels if you have a lot of magic power. With about level\n30 characters I would recommend. The upper part can be beaten with level 10+ characters,\nbecause it mainly contains the Ruffinas and Thugs which are easy to kill.\nx - marks a spot where you can find a treasure chest or the likes\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/dragoons-caverns-pic.jpg","CastleIronfist/dragoons-caverns-shot.jpg","CastleIronfist/dragoons-caverns.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/dragoons-caverns.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-shadow-guild-hideout","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Shadow Guild Hideout","body":"Castle Ironfist : Shadow Guild Hideout\nThis area appears to be abandoned. However, fresh footprints\nlead in and out from a recently repaired door. Perhaps it isn't\nso abandoned after all.\n 1  Secret Door, open it from the West side.\n 2  Locked Room with Sharry Carnegie (quest item :) inside. Click a small key on the door to open it; the key is in one of the many chests.\n 3  Letter from the Price of Thieves.\n 4  Key to the locked room.\nHit switch a and the b to get over to 4 to get the key to get into room 2.\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/shadow-guild-hideout-pic.jpg","CastleIronfist/shadow-guild-hideout-shot.jpg","CastleIronfist/shadow-guild-hideout.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/shadow-guild-hideout.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-small-town","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Small Town","body":"Castle Ironfist : Small Town\nArea below the Castle Ironfist\n 1  Tavern: The King's Crown (fill to\n20)\nDagger Expert in the back.\n 2  Docks: Zephyr [Travel Schedule]\n 3  Expert Bowmanship (Helen Teal)\nMind Guild Membership (Tracy Fauta the Apprentice)\n 4  [Retrieve Harp Quest] --- Berserkers' Fury Membership\n 5  Berserkers' Fury, Skills: Bow, Shield, Chain, Plate and Repair\n 6  Weapon: The Eagle's Eye\n 7  Stables: Royal Lines [Travel Schedule]\n 8  Armor: Metalweave Armory\n 9  Expert Shield Defense\n 10  Expert Leather Armor Training\n 11  Expert Plate Armor Training\n 12  Expert Chain Armor Training\n17:48\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/small-town.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/small-town.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-snergles-caverns","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Snergle's Caverns","body":"Castle Ironfist : Snergle's Caverns\nThese caverns once belonged to the exiled King Rocklin,\nbut now they are home to the new Dwarven King Snergle.\n 1  Waterfall, holds a unique item, save before using SPACE bar and you will be reward with a powerful item if you try long enought.\n 2  Door to Snergle, requires key - below for more info.\n 3  Level on chair, opens #4\n 4  Locked door, press lever at #3 to open.\n 5  Bones: +5 migth permanently\n 6  Bones: Teleport you back to main entrance.\nNote: The door at the end of the dungeon can only be opened with the correct key.\nThe key can be found in Mire of the Damned in the Snergle's Iron Mines in.\nOnce you open the door, be prepared for 20+ Dwarfs popping up behind you in the tunnel you came from.\nOh, and lets not forget the 50+ Darfs in the room you just opened. :) Note that the Dwarf Lords can break your armor,\nso a constant repairing is advised.\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/snergles-caverns-pic.jpg","CastleIronfist/snergles-caverns-shot.jpg","CastleIronfist/snergles-caverns.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/snergles-caverns.html"},{"id":"castleironfist-temple-of-baa","region":"Castle Ironfist","title":"Temple of Baa","body":"Castle Ironfist : Temple of Baa\nFaint chanting can be heard from beyond the doors of this Temple.\nVisitors do not appear to be welcome here.\n 1    Door Puzzle, open doors in this order: N,E,W,S\nNote: Be prepared for an encounter with 20+ skelletons and 10 Magicans\nChest contains key to secret room.\n 2  Gong on table, Lawrence Aleman in Free Haven gives you 2,000 gold for it. Secret room to the East (requires key from #1.), it splits into two tunnels and leads to two more secret doors.\nTrigger Area for 50+ skeletons\n 3  Secret room with chest and instrument (quest item) key for room 4\n 4  Secret room with 30+ gold pouches\n 5  The store room key. Click on the statue.\n 6  The store room. The Bathouse key is in here.\n 7  The Bathhouse, The Store Room Key is in the chest.\n 8  Store Room, Secret room key\n 9  The second bathhouse the chest contains the key to the Treasure room at 3\nNote: there is a hidden treasure in on of the torches between 4, and 2, in the hallway between them.\nLeave us a message at mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on .","images":["CastleIronfist/temple-of-baa-pic.jpg","CastleIronfist/temple-of-baa-shot.jpg","CastleIronfist/temple-of-baa.gif"],"sourcePath":"CastleIronfist/temple-of-baa.html"},{"id":"dragonsand-location","region":"Dragonsand","title":"Dragonsand","body":"Places : Dragonsand\n1. Tomb of VARN\n2. The pirates treasure, this is where you come when you have read all of the obelisks\n3. Obelisk #6\n4. Shrine of Gods (+20 to all stats permanently!)\nNW wall will take you to the NWC dungeon.\n5. +50 Hit Points\n6. +10 to all resistance permanent\n7. +10 to seven primary stats\n8. The Tent Village of Dragonsands\nA pedestal for the Place Statues Quest\n X  Nice treasure chests. All trapped","images":["Dragonsand/land.jpg"],"sourcePath":"Dragonsand/location.html"},{"id":"dragonsand-dragonsand","region":"Dragonsand","title":"City Map","body":"Dragonsand : City Map\n1. NPC: +15% experience, takes 7% gold\nNPC: +6 merchant, takes 2% gold\n2. NPC: +4 all spell skills, takes 20% gold\nNPC: cast's Town Portal once per day, takes 20% gold\n3. NPC: cast's Water Walk once per day, takes 20% gold\nNPC: cast's Fly once per day, takes 10% gold\n4. Abdul himself!\n5. Trades Pyramids, or Keg's for Armor\n6. NPC: +20 to all elemental resistances, takes 20% gold\nNPC: Heals and Cures everything once per day, takes 50% gold\n7. A pedestal for the Place Statues Quest\n8. Trades Pyramids, or Keg's for Weapons\n9. NPC: +4 merchant skill, takes 1% gold\nNPC: 3 skill to all weapons, takes 4% gold\n10. rades Pyramids, or Keg's for Accessories\n11. +20% all found gold, takes 10% gold\nNPC: +8 diplomacy, takes 3% gold\n12. Trade Lamps for Gems","images":["Dragonsand/dragonsand.jpg"],"sourcePath":"Dragonsand/dragonsand.html"},{"id":"dragonsand-tomb-of-varn","region":"Dragonsand","title":"Tomb of VARN","body":"Dragonsand : Tomb of VARN\nThis pyramid seems to be made of a strange weathered metal. It appears to be partially burried in the sand.\n1. Entrance\n2. Backdoor Key\n3. Backdoor\n4. Center of pyramid. On the main floor, there are the pools that you walk onto to be prompted to enter a name. On the floor above, there is an elevator that takes you to a room at the top of the pyramid.\n5. Water Temple Key\nFirst Mates Code\n6. Water Temple\nIn the bottom you will find another crystal skull, and the Bibliothecca Chest key.\nNavigator's Scroll\n7. The Flame Door Key, and a crystal skull\nThe Captain's Scroll\n8. Control Cube\n9. Biblotheca (Libarary) Chest in the librarym there are books in the book cases.\nThe Doctors's Code is in the chest\nThe Engeneer's Code is in the wall on the right as you face the chest.\nThe Communications Officer is in the wall on the left as you face the chest.\n10. You can find some Magic Lamps here. You can trade them in Dragonsand city\nThis place could be a city in itself. There is the main pyramid, and the central pyramid inside of it. There are plenty of Efferts in here, and many guards of VARN. They all have less than 1,000 HP, but they have some magical immunities. Implosion seemd to work on all of them though.\nThe crystal skull will protect you when you get into the main room in the central pyramid (#4 in the main level) from the radiation that will hit you quite often. Once you are radiated you can just go get in some of the water to stop the damage. Until you enter again. The skull seems to only be 100% protection for those holding it.\nI kind of thought it was cool the passwords you have to enter are from the original Star Trek only backwards. Plan on spending some time on this one.","images":["Dragonsand/tomb-of-varn-pic.jpg","Dragonsand/tomb-of-varn-shot1.jpg","Dragonsand/tomb-of-varn-shot2.jpg","Dragonsand/tomb-of-varn.gif"],"sourcePath":"Dragonsand/tomb-of-varn.html"},{"id":"eelinfestedwaters-location","region":"Eel Infested Waters","title":"Eel Infested Waters","body":"Place : Eel Infested Waters\nThere is a small city here, the Alamos, and the normal Shirne, and Obelisk.\n 1.  The City\n 2. Alamos [Map]\n 3. +20 to Elemntal Resistances, temporary.\n 4. Obelisk #13\n 5. Shrine of Poison [Shrine List] pray here in November\n 6. A Stone's Throw, (Inn), Light Magic Master in the back (Saintly Reputation, and expert)\n 7. +20 to Magic Resistance, temporary.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["EelInfestedWaters/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"EelInfestedWaters/location.html"},{"id":"eelinfestedwaters-eelinfestedwaters","region":"Eel Infested Waters","title":"City Map","body":"Eel Infested Waters : City Map\nEel Infested Waters\n 1.  Abdual's Discount House of Worship\n 2. Little Charms\n 3. Ancient Weapons Expert\n 4. An Arrow's Flight Inn\n 5. Alamos [ Map ]\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["EelInfestedWaters/EelInfestedWaters.gif"],"sourcePath":"EelInfestedWaters/EelInfestedWaters.html"},{"id":"eelinfestedwaters-alamos","region":"Eel Infested Waters","title":"The Alamos","body":"Eel Infested Waters : The Alamos\nThe first fortress dedicated to magical research, its remote location provided\nsecrecy for the mages and protection for the populace in the event of an accident.\nAlamos, Eel Infested Waters\n 1.  Entrance\n 2. The Memoy Crystal Beta is here. The password is JBARD\n 3. A lot of good treasures, books, gems, gold.\n 4. A transporter to Silver Cove.\nThere are a ton of ememies here, Wizards, Matrons, and Air Elemntals. To totally clean out this dungeon will take a while. It is one of the biggest around.\nI would suggest that you have Lloyd's beacon, use it and go to New Sorpigal to heal yourself, you wil need to often. The teleporter requires a key that you find in a chest. Some doors will not open without you having the guy carrying the memory crystal highlighted.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["EelInfestedWaters/Alamos-pic.jpg","EelInfestedWaters/Alamos-shot.jpg","EelInfestedWaters/Alamos.gif"],"sourcePath":"EelInfestedWaters/Alamos.html"},{"id":"freehaven-location","region":"Free Haven","title":"Free Haven","body":"Free Haven\nA nice city that has just about everything, two of some things. It seems to be surrounded by magicians.\nArea of Free Haven\nCity Map\nDragoon's Keep\nTemple of the Moon\nTomb of Ethric the Mad\nSewers\nOracle\nControl Center\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":[],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/location.html"},{"id":"freehaven-freehaven","region":"Free Haven","title":"City Map","body":"Free Haven: City Map\nFree Haven\n1. Water Magic Expert $1000\n2. Fire Magic Expert $1000\n3. Expert Earth / Expert Air $1000\n4. Expert Plate Training $2000\n5. Adept Guild of the Mind\n6. Expert Shield Defense $2000\n7. The Sharpening Stone Weapons\n8. Duelist's Edge\n9. Disarm Expert $500/Smugglers Guild Membership\n10. Air Guild Membership\n11. Fire Guild Membership\n12. Abdual's Discount Goods\n13. Duelist's Edge Guild Membership 50\n14. Quest , rescue Sherell at the Temple of Tsantsa\n15. Keg's $300\n16. Sewer Entrance Tooth Collector $500\n17. Bank\n18. Training Academy\n19. The Sorcerors Shoppe\n20. Adept Guild of the Spirit\n21. Achemy and Incantations\n22. Expert Sword $2000 and Expert Knife $2000\n23. Adept Guild of the Earth\n24. Adept Guild of the Body\n25. Buy's Gong's $2000\n26. Expert Merchant Training\n27. Quest for the Mordred Dagger by Zoltan Phelps\n28. Expert Diplomacy\n29. Fire Guild Membership\n30. Air Guild Membership\n31. A Bard\n32. Heidi Strumper\n33. Earth Guild Membership\n34. Water Guild Membership\n35. Echoing Wisper Inn Cheapest\n36. Harpy Feathers 10 gold each\n37. Sewer Entrance\n38. Indentification Master 7 Skill and 30 intellect\n39. High Council / Oracle / Control Center\n40. Buy's Amber for $500\n41. Buy's Four Leaf Clover $25\n42. Adept Guild of the Air\n43. Adept Guild of Fire\n44. Free Haven Travel\n45. The Footman's Friend\n46. Feather And Strings\n47. Victor's Hall\n48. Membership to Guild of the Air $50\n49. Spirit Guild Membership $50\n50. Mind Guild Membership $50\n51. Body Magic Expert / Spirit Magic Expert $2000\n52. Mind Magic Expert $2000\n53. Adept Guild of Water\n54. Free Haven Temple as part of the Repair Temple Quest\n55. George Almond The Stone Cutter also see the Repair Temple Quest\n56. Shrine of Accuracy\n57.\nRal the carpenter also see the Repair Temple Quest\nLeave me a mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on May the 6th in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/FreeHaven.jpg"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/FreeHaven.html"},{"id":"freehaven-control-center","region":"Free Haven","title":"Control Center","body":"Free Haven : Control Center\n1. Entrance\n2. Read the sign on the wall to get the Blaster Skill (Ancient Weapon)\nX Chests where you can find Blasters and or Blaster Rifles\nThis is VERY tough. The Terminators will eradicate you. You can get this fiexd by casting resurection, or visiting the Temple you resotred in Free Haven . They only have 1080 Hit points, but seem to be pretty stong in defense just like the Oracle said. Blasters do some damage. I had my skill up to 10 Masters, and was only doing 25-30 damage. Inferno was working well as was Implostion. But level 20 Master. Once you get enough weapons to supply your party, you can leave, or not bother to get them all some. There are some chest's that have a bunch of memory crystals, and control cubes, they are the two right most ones. But they are useless.\nLeave me a mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/control-center.jpg"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/control-center.html"},{"id":"freehaven-dragoon","region":"Free Haven","title":"Dragoon's Keep","body":"Free Haven: Dragoon's Keep\nDragoon's Keep\n1. Entrance\n2. This is the main chamber, this is also where you will find the Mordred Dagger, that is the lost arifact that Zoltan Phelps from Free Haven is seeking.\nThere is not much worth noting here except for the dagger. The Keep is full of Armored Knights, and rats. I believe the verterans have just over 200 hit points a peice.\nI suggest you return the dagger, even though it is very nice, and quite valuable (20,000). Zoltan gives it back anyway.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/keep.gif"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/dragoon.html"},{"id":"freehaven-oracle","region":"Free Haven","title":"Oracle of Enroth","body":"Free Haven : Oracle of Enroth\n1. Entrance\n2. The Oracle of Enroth, and the entrance to the Control Center\nLeave me a mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/oracle.jpg"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/oracle.html"},{"id":"freehaven-sewer","region":"Free Haven","title":"Sewers","body":"Free Haven: Sewers\nSewers of Free Haven\n1. This is where you will find the Prince of Thieves that Lord Stone in White Cap is looking for.\n2. This is the great tressure room of the sewer, some say the key is randomly placed that opens this door.\n3. This room is a transport room to the Supreme Temple of Baa.\nThis map has many round sewer gates on some of the wall. If you search those sewer gates,\nyou will find multiple times a few gold coins. Note that you will not see\nthat gold laying on the ground, so search all gates to find the right one.\nThis is also the exact same place where you CAN find the treasure room key. Note that\nI say CAN because it is rather random. Once you find that place with the gold, load\nthe game again and walk to that exact same gate and save before searching.\nNow search until you stop finding gold. If you have not found the key yet,\nload the game and search again. This might take multiple tries, but you will find\nthe treasure room key eventually.\nNote: If you have already completed this dungeons\nand searched the sewer gates without success. Then you will have to wait till the\nmap re-spawns in order to search again. This can take up to a full game year from\nthe first time you entered the dungeon.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/sewer.gif"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/sewer.html"},{"id":"freehaven-freehaven0","region":"Free Haven","title":"Surrounding area","body":"Free Haven : Surrounding area\n1. Temple of the moon, Dungeon [ Map ]\n2. Well, it will make fire archers appear.\n3. Rockham's Pride, you will also find Chadwick here.\n4. Town of Free Haven\n5. Lighthouse\n6. Tomb of Ethric the Mad [ Map ]\n7. Obelisk\n8. Temple of Baa\n9. Dragoon's Keep [ Map ]\n10. Castle Temper, home of Lord Osric Temper. Master Plate on the top.\n11. Shrine of Accuracy\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/FreeHaven0.gif"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/FreeHaven0.html"},{"id":"freehaven-moon","region":"Free Haven","title":"Temple of the Moon","body":"Free Haven: Temple of the Moon\nTemple of the Moon\n1. Entrance\n2. Shrine of Life\n3. Shrine of Accuracy\n4. Shrine of Might\n5. Shrine of Endurance\n6. Shrine of Speed\nThere is a switch on the back of the shrine to to the small room.\n7. Shrine of Luck\n8. Shrine of the Moon\nThere are more snakes in this one. There are Medusas, they can stone you but only at close range. There are some tough Druids hanging around also so I'd recommend some protection from poison, fire, and magic.\nThere is a plaque over the door to the Moon Shrine that reads Life above all, Accuracy before Might, Endurance before Speed, and finally Luck. This is the order to visit the shrines, to open the door, and get +5 to each of these stats for each character!\nPoints 2,3,4,5,6,7\nThere is also a letter in the small room behind the Speed shrine that someone might want, but I am not sure yet.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/moon.gif"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/moon.html"},{"id":"freehaven-ethric","region":"Free Haven","title":"Tomb of Ethric the Mad","body":"Free Haven: Tomb of Ethric the Mad\nTomb of Ethric the Mad\n1. Entrance\n2. This room is criss crossed by fire balls, but if you time it right you can run straight across.\n3. The liche Ethric the Mad, you need his skull for Gabriel Cartman .\nThis tomb is full of liche's and ghost's of all kinds. The coffins contain treasure. The Skull is a quest item. You will want some good magic protection in here.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["FreeHaven/tomb.gif"],"sourcePath":"FreeHaven/ethric.html"},{"id":"whitecap-location","region":"Frozen Highlands","title":"Frozen Highlands","body":"Place : White Cap\nThis city seems to be divided into three parts by a mountain range. Many masters can be found in this area though.\n 1    White Cap [City Map]\n 2 The Castle of Eric Von Stromgaurd [City Map]\n 3 Castle Stone [City Map]\n 4 IceWind Keep [Map]\n 5 Shadow Guild [Map]\n 6 Shrine of Endurance [Shrine List] pray here in April\n 7 Obelisk #7\n 8 Fountain [+20 accuracy and speed boost]\n 9 Fountain [+20 armor boost]\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["WhiteCap/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"WhiteCap/location.html"},{"id":"whitecap-castle","region":"Frozen Highlands","title":"Castle and Courtyard","body":"White Cap : Castle and Courtyard\nWhite Cap\n 1.  Bow Expert (4 Skill, 2,000 Gold) / Expert Mace Training (4 Skill, 2,000 Gold)\n 2. Well +30 to Might Temporarily\n 3. Shrine of Endurance (visit in April)\n 4. Castle of Eric Von Stromgaurd, Quest to stop winter, and The Battle Mage Quests to find a key. Master of Diplomacy on the roof (7 Skill, 200 Fame, 2,500 Gold)\n 5. Well +10 to Level Temporarily\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["WhiteCap/Castle.gif"],"sourcePath":"WhiteCap/Castle.html"},{"id":"whitecap-whitecap1","region":"Frozen Highlands","title":"Castle Stone City Map","body":"White Cap : Castle Stone City Map\nWhite Cap\n 1.  Well +10 to Level Temporarily\n 2. Quality Armor\n 3. Haft and Handle Pole Arms\n 4. Master Leather Armor (10 Skill 3,000 Gold)\nLord Anthony Stone, Cleric Quest to become a Priest, the Quest to become a High Priest, and the Quest , to capture the Prince of thieves.\nMaster Knife (10 Skill, 40 Speed, 5,000 Gold)\n 5. Master Disarm Training (7 Skill, 40 Accuracy, 2,500 Gold)\n 6. Rime and Reason Inn\n 7. Protective Services Membership 50 Gold\n 6. Repair Mastery (7 Skill, 40 Accuracy, 2,500 Gold)\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["WhiteCap/WhiteCap1.gif"],"sourcePath":"WhiteCap/WhiteCap1.html"},{"id":"whitecap-whitecap","region":"Frozen Highlands","title":"City Map","body":"White Cap : City Map\nWhite Cap\n 1.  Elemental Guild Membership 100 Gold\n 2. Dark Guild Membership 1,000 Gold\n 3. Riverside Academy\n 4. Blades End\n 5. Silver Lining Armor & Shield\n 6. +5 Might Permanent, it does kill you to drink from it though.\n 7. Adept Guild of the Elements\n 8. Bank\n 9. General Store\n 10. The Frosty Tankard Inn\n 11. White Cap Temple\n 12. Initiate Guild of Dark\n 13. White Cap Transport Company\n 14. +5 Endurance Permanent, it kills you also.\n 15. Apples, Thorns, and Potions\n 16. Mark and Missile\n 17. Dark Magic Expert (4 Skill, 2,000 Gold)\n 18. Blade's End Membership 50 Gold\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["WhiteCap/WhiteCap.gif"],"sourcePath":"WhiteCap/WhiteCap.html"},{"id":"whitecap-icewind-keep","region":"Frozen Highlands","title":"IceWind Keep","body":"White Cap : IceWind Keep\nOriginally used to keep creatures from escaping the Frozen Wastelands, now the\nkeep prevents traffic to and from Castle Stormgard and town of White Cap.\nIceWindKeep\n 1.  Entrance\n 2. Switch 1 of 2\n 3. Switch 2 if 2\n 4. The Switch is in the arm of the chair on the right.\n 5. The key's to the Dragon Towers are in here.\nThis one is not really that tricky. As you enter you have flip the two switches at the end of each hall way, that will open the big door that you see right at first. Go throught that area to the throne room, and flip the switch on the arm of the chair to get entrance to the treasure room 5.\nDon't forget to check the beds.\nNOTE: If you are not sure if you can handle all the guy's that will be in the big room, and there are a LOT of them, before you throw the second switch go stand by the big door and cast Ring of Fire a few times to kill some off and damage most of them.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["WhiteCap/IceWind-Keep-pic.jpg","WhiteCap/IceWind-Keep-shot.jpg","WhiteCap/IceWind-Keep.gif"],"sourcePath":"WhiteCap/IceWind-Keep.html"},{"id":"whitecap-shadow-guild","region":"Frozen Highlands","title":"Shadow Guild","body":"White Cap : Shadow Guild\nHome to the so-called Prince of Thieves, the Shadow Guild operates outside of\nAnthony Stone's jurisdiction. This Guildhall is not open to the public.\nShadow Guild\n 1.  Entrance\n 2. Note stating that the Prince has moved to Free Haven sewers.\nTo activate the teleporter: Stand at the entry of the door, facing north.\nNow notice the darker tiles on the floor, jump on those in a half left circle\ntill you reach the opposite side of the entry wall. If you do it right,\nyou will hear a click each time you jump on the tile. Then you will be teleported.\n 3. A teleporter will open after you did the \"jump-play\" in room 2.\n 4. You will be teleported into this room by using the teleporter from room 3. This room has four riddles.\nBehind each door you will find a teleporter:\nNorth: Free Haven\nSouth: Dragoon's Caverns (Castle Ironfist)\nWest: Back to entry of cave\nEast: Shadow Guild Hideout (Castle Ironfist)\nIf you have high enough perception you can see all of the floor tiles that will set off traps.There are many of them.\nThe Prince is actually in the Sewers of Free Haven but I'll get a map up soon.\nRiddles\nNorth Alive without breath, as cold as death, never thirsty\never drinking, all in mail never clinking, ever travelling, never\nwalking, mouth ever moving, never talking. What am I?\nFISH\nSouth What consumes rocks, levels mountains, destroys wood,\npushes the clouds across the sky, and can make a young one old?\nTIME\nWest I go through an apple, or point your way, I fit in a\nbow, then a target, to stay. What am I?\nARROW\nEast You cannot see me, hear me or touch me. I lie behind\nthe stars and alter what is real, I am what you really fear, Close your eyes and I near.\nWhat am I?\nDARK\nThanks goes to Ulf-Andre Gramstad for pointing out the teleporter in room #2.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["WhiteCap/ShadowGuild-pic.jpg","WhiteCap/ShadowGuild-shot.jpg","WhiteCap/ShadowGuild.gif"],"sourcePath":"WhiteCap/Shadow-Guild.html"},{"id":"hermitsisle-location","region":"Hermit's Isle","title":"Hermit's Isle","body":"Places : Hermits Isle\nNot a nice place to visit even.\n1. Obelisk #3\n2. Fountain of Rejuvenation\n3. A pair of Chests\n4. Supreme Temple of Baa","images":["HermitsIsle/land.jpg"],"sourcePath":"HermitsIsle/location.html"},{"id":"hermitsisle-supreme-temple-of-baa","region":"Hermit's Isle","title":"Supreme Temple of Baa","body":"Hermit's Isle : Supreme Temple of Baa\nThe temperature rises steadily as you approach the doors, the smell of sulfur and ash are strong. This place resembles a hideout more than a temple.\n1. Entrance\n2. Portal to Free Haven Sewere\n3. Memory Crystal Alpha , you can also see Slicker Silvertounge here.\nThis one is really quite easy, getting here is the hard part. There are some clerics, some devils, and a few fire elementals.","images":["HermitsIsle/supreme-temple-of-baa-pic.jpg","HermitsIsle/supreme-temple-of-baa-shot.jpg","HermitsIsle/supreme-temple-of-baa.jpg"],"sourcePath":"HermitsIsle/supreme-temple-of-baa.html"},{"id":"kriegspire-location","region":"Kriegspire","title":"Kriegspire","body":"Place : Kriegspire\n1  \nSuperior Temple of Baa\n[\nMap\n]\n2 Fountain: +5 permanent elemental (fire, electricity, cold and poison)\n3  \nAgar's Laboratory\n[\nMap\n]\n4 Shrine of Cold\n5 Hermit\nwill End Winter for the the\n[\nEnd Winter Quest ]\n6 Obelisk #4\n7  \nCave of the Dragon Riders\n[\nMap\n]\n8  \nDevil Outpost (Demon Lair)\n[\nMap\n]\n9 Fountain: +40 Armor class\n10 Shrine of Fire ( August )\n11  \nCastle Kriegspire\n[\nMap\n]\nMaster Bowmen on top of castle\n12  \nKriegspire City\n[\nMap\n]\n13 Pedestal\n[\nPlace Statues Quest ]","images":["Kriegspire/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"Kriegspire/location.html"},{"id":"kriegspire-agars-laboratory","region":"Kriegspire","title":"Agar's Laboratory","body":"Kriegspire : Agar's Laboratory\nThis laboratory is the birthplace for countless horrid experiements. Its location was\nchosen for both safety and secrecy.\n1. Switch #1, releases a few flying eyes.\n2. Switch #2, releases a few flying eyes.\n3. Wall opens if switch #1 and #2 are pressed. The switch on top of the stone table can be pressed but its function is unknown to me. If you touch the\nblue ground infront of it, the button will become unpressed again.\n4. Switch\n5. Switch with same behaviour as described above in #3.\n6. Empty chest, some eye monsters will come from the little passage if you go near the chest.\n7. Agar himself, easy to kill, but protected with some eyes. You find a scroll in the left most chest.\n8. Exit from the dungeon.\nYou will find quite a few Flying Eyes and Agar Pet Birds. Take one room at a time\nand use the Heroism spell as often as possible. An nice way to kill the flying eyes,\nwhich are released by pressing the switches, is to cast wizard eye and then kill\nthe monsters through the floor with your bows.\nWhile walking around, search and you will find some crystals and other things.","images":["Kriegspire/agars-laboratory-pic.jpg","Kriegspire/agars-laboratory-shot.jpg","Kriegspire/agars-laboratory.gif"],"sourcePath":"Kriegspire/agars-laboratory.html"},{"id":"kriegspire-castle-kriegspire","region":"Kriegspire","title":"Castle Kriegspire","body":"Kriegspire : Castle Kriegspire\nKriegspire no longer rest's between it's lakes, the earth around the castle was raised to preven the creatures inside from escaping.\n1. Entrance\n2. Memory Crystal Epsilon\nneeded for the [\nFind Memory Crystal Epsilon Quest ]\n3. This chest has great stuff in it.\n4. Lurch (2,000 hit points)\n5. Roland's Journal, in the cage.\n6. Jeweled Egg\n7. The Guardian of Kriegspire, warps you to 8\nThere are a few Drakes in here, but mostly Minitaurs. This one is pretty straight forward, no multiple switch tricks or anything. Lurch is the strongest guy in here, and he only had abot 1900 hit points.","images":["Kriegspire/castle-kriegspire-out.jpg","Kriegspire/castle-kriegspire-pic.jpg","Kriegspire/castle-kriegspire-shot.jpg","Kriegspire/castle-kriegspire.jpg"],"sourcePath":"Kriegspire/castle-kriegspire.html"},{"id":"kriegspire-cave-of-the-dragon-riders","region":"Kriegspire","title":"Cave of the Dragon Riders","body":"Kriegspire : Cave of the Dragon Riders\nThese caves house a strange alliance between human warriors and dragons.\nThe Dragon Towers were built in the towns to ward off these raiders.\nThere really is not point to this dungeon except fighting.\nThis cave sure is the most curved and sloped of all. You find lots of Wyrms, Death and\nDoom Knights, and even more powerful Cuisinarts. Better be around level 60 or you will\nspend more time healing yourself then fighting. :)\nYou will find many nice items here, chain and plate armors, all kinds of weapons, rings and gold.","images":["Kriegspire/cave-of-the-dragon-riders-pic.jpg","Kriegspire/cave-of-the-dragon-riders-shot.jpg","Kriegspire/cave-of-the-dragon-riders.jpg"],"sourcePath":"Kriegspire/cave-of-the-dragon-riders.html"},{"id":"kriegspire-city","region":"Kriegspire","title":"City Map","body":"Kriegspire : City Map\n1. Tavern: The Broken Promise ( fills for 20 days )\n2. Fountain: +30 level temporary\n3. Training: Lone Tree Training\n4. NPC: heals and cures party once a day, takes 50% of gold -- what a joke!\n5. NPC: +4 points to merchant and diplomacy skills, takes 5% of gold.\n6. Weapons: Knight's Paradise\n7. NPC: +5 points to luck and takes 1% gold.\n8. NPC: casts Heroism once a day at master level and takes 3% gold.\n9. Fountain: drops you right into the middle of the Castle Kriegspire dungeon.\n10. Fountain: +10 permanent magic resistance, Eradicates character\n11. Emil Lime\nthe Enchanter gives you the [Find Egg Quest] .\n12. Armor: Armorworks\n13. NPC: all map crossings one day faster, takes 1% gold\n14. Fire Tower\n15. NPC: +10% experience, takes 3% gold\n16. General Stores: Unusual Enchantments\n17. Stables: King's Highway [Travel Schedule]\n18. NPC: cures party once a day, takes 20% gold\n19. Fountain: trades 5,000 gold into 5,000 experience\n20. NPC: +15% experience, takes 7% gold\n21. NPC: +4 points to diplomacy, takes 2% gold\n22. Unknown Stone Tower\n23. Expert Light Magic","images":["Kriegspire/city.gif"],"sourcePath":"Kriegspire/city.html"},{"id":"kriegspire-devil-outpost","region":"Kriegspire","title":"Devil Outpost","body":"Kriegspire : Devil Outpost\nThe faint smell of brimstone and the sound of creatures talking in a strange\nlanguage drift from the entrance of this cave.\nBesides finding a handfull of Devil enemies, you can pick up a message scroll from\nthe corpse of the Devil of Baa. The scroll is needed to complete the [\nDevils' Outpost\nQuest ]","images":["Kriegspire/devil-outpost-pic.jpg","Kriegspire/devil-outpost-shot.jpg","Kriegspire/devil-outpost.gif"],"sourcePath":"Kriegspire/devil-outpost.html"},{"id":"kriegspire-superior-temple-of-baa","region":"Kriegspire","title":"Superior Temple of Baa","body":"Kriegspire : Superior Temple of Baa\nThe focal point of all Baa worship in Enroth, the Superior Temple only allows followers of Baa inside.\n1   Pedestal: Expert Perception is the key, and the doors of Baa will let you be.\nThe spiral then each head, talk to Baa, or you'll be dead.\nThis means that you need a high perception to open the doors, an expert at least (8 Perception).\n2 Letter from Zenofex needed to finish the Find Cure quest.\nyou need the High Sorcerers Key and High Clerics Key to open it.\n3 You will find the High Sorcerers Key here.\n4 You will find the High Clerics Key here.\n5 This is the loop the poem talks about, sparks rain from the ceiling.\n6 Here you will find 4 heads of baa 1-4\n7 The Almighty Head of Baa\nThis is not too complex of a dungeon which is nice. There are plenty of Wizards and Clerics to fight.\nTo get into this place you need to be wearing the Cloak of Baa you got from Wilbur Humphrey's from the Find Cure for Slicker Silvertoung .\nThen you need do is pick up the key's, then the chest will open for you. In the room the chest is in there is a pedestal with a note on it that in a roundabout way tells you you need to have high percerption to open the doors, or get shocked. I put on the cloak that Humphrey's gave me on my guy with the highest perception. 8 skill and an expert status.\nAn interesting side \"quest\", you can become a member of the Temple of Baa by going around the tunnel by 5, and then going to the chapel at 6, and touching the heads in order. You can then go and click on the Supreme Head of Baa to become a member. I got 50,000 experience, a Bad reputation, and whatever benifts are derived from this. But the effects seem to vary, some say they lost 2,000,000 experience, some said their reputation was unaffected.","images":["Kriegspire/superior-temple-of-baa-pic.jpg","Kriegspire/superior-temple-of-baa-shot.jpg","Kriegspire/superior-temple-of-baa.jpg"],"sourcePath":"Kriegspire/superior-temple-of-baa.html"},{"id":"mireofthedamned-location","region":"Mire of the Damned","title":"Mire of the Damned","body":"Mire of the Damned\nThe home of Ghosts and Spirits, be prepared for a mess, you might age\ninto certain death.\nLand Map\nCity Map\nDragon's Lair\nSnergle's Iron Mines\nCastle Darkmoor\nShrine of Speed (NW in center region)","images":[],"sourcePath":"MireOfTheDamned/location.html"},{"id":"mireofthedamned-castle-darkmoor","region":"Mire of the Damned","title":"Castle Darkmoor","body":"Mire of the Damned : Castle Darkmoor\nThis laboratory is the birthplace for countless horrid experiements. Its location was\nchosen for both safety and secrecy.\n1. Entrance\n2. Hitting this switch will turn the cube at 3 red.\n3. This is a large cube hanging in the room. You have to touch it to open up more passages.\n4. This large cube will drop lame swords and teleport you around.\n5. Go up the ramp. There is a secret door here.\n6. hit this switch and return to #4 and touch the cube again, this will lower the shield at #7\n7. Invisible barrier, see #6\n8. Memory Crystal Delta\n9. Read the plaque. Then tough the cube to be transported to 10.\n10. You will find the Quest Item Book of Liches here.\nThis is a pretty tough one. The \"flying eye's\" as most people call them will cast Dispel Magic, Insanity, and Fear. You'll just have to battle through them. Here are a few hints:\nTerrible Eye: These are immune to fire attacks, Implosion seems to work vell however.\nFlying Eye: These are immune to water, Inceinerate works well, as does Implosion.\nThe others seem to have no definate immunities so just use your strongest spell, It seems they are all weak against poisons though, so try Toxic Cloud or Acid Burst.\nOnce you enter, and touch the cube at 3, you can then hit the switch at 2. Touch the cube again, and the back of the dungeon opens. You can go to 4 and clear this room out, or go directly to 5 and start toward 6. There is no way from the room that 4 is in to get to 6, Now I know get the memory crystal, and read teh plaque. You will be warped to chamber 8, you'll find the book of Liches here, and some dead people. You may take things from them, but you will lose one full reputation level.","images":["MireOfTheDamned/castle-darkmoor-pic.jpg","MireOfTheDamned/castle-darkmoor-shot.jpg","MireOfTheDamned/castle-darkmoor.gif"],"sourcePath":"MireOfTheDamned/castle-darkmoor.html"},{"id":"mireofthedamned-city","region":"Mire of the Damned","title":"Darkmoor City Map","body":"Mire of the Damned: Darkmoor City Map\n1. Tavern: The Haunt fill for 14 days\nAvinril Smythers [Defeat Snergle Quest]\n2. Armor: Mailed fist Armory\n3. Master Spear Training (req: rank 8 and Cavalier status)\n4. NPC: +15% experience and takes %7 gold\n5. Expert Axe Fighting\n6. Expert Merchant Training\n7. House of no importance\n8. NPC: +2 points to all weapon skill and takes 3% gold\n9. General Store: Smoke and Mirrors\n10. NPC: +5 points in perception, +10 in luck and takes 4% gold\n11. Terry Ros the Spell Master [Destroy Book Quest]\n12. NPC: casts Water Walk once a day and takes 10% gold\n13. NPC: makes one food per day and takes 3% gold\n14. NPC: +4 points diplomancy and takes 2% gold\n15. Expert Mace Training\n16. NPC: +4 points all magic skills and takes 20%\n17. Weapons: Blunt Trauma Weapons\nMaster Chain Armor Training - next door (reg: rank 10 and Crusader status)\n18. Master Perception Training (reg: rank 7, luck 30)\n19. Stables: Darkmoor Travel","images":["MireOfTheDamned/city.gif"],"sourcePath":"MireOfTheDamned/city.html"},{"id":"mireofthedamned-dragons-lair","region":"Mire of the Damned","title":"Dragon's Lair","body":"Mire of the Damned: Dragon's Lair\nRecommended character level: 30+\nHere you will find Longfang Witherhide from the [Slay Dragon Quest].\nYou need some decent fire protection but some even better armor. If you do not come close to him he will only\nuse his long range fire ball which is does not hit very hard. So run into the cave and into a corner and switch into Turn-Based mode,\nthen if he comes to close, go into Real-Time mode and go into another corner.\nAfter you kill him, search his dead body and take with you the Dragon Claw, which you will need to\ncomplete the quest.","images":["MireOfTheDamned/dragons-lair.gif"],"sourcePath":"MireOfTheDamned/dragons-lair.html"},{"id":"mireofthedamned-land","region":"Mire of the Damned","title":"Land Map","body":"Mire of the Damned: Land Map\n1. Dragon's Lair [Map]\n2. Castle Darkmoor\n3. Tavern: The Rusted Shield, fills for 10 days\n4. Circus Location\n5. Darkmoor [City Map]\n6. Snergle's Iron Mines [Map]\n7. Obelisk #9\n8. Shrine of Speed pray here in the month of June\n9. Fountain of endurance\n10. Pedestal\n10. Temple of Baa, healing and donations\nx - marks a spot where you can find a treasure chest or the likes","images":["MireOfTheDamned/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"MireOfTheDamned/land.html"},{"id":"mireofthedamned-snergles-iron-mines","region":"Mire of the Damned","title":"Snergle's Iron Mines","body":"Mire of the Damned: Snergle's Iron Mines\nRecommended character level: 25+\n1. Cell Key\n2. Ghim Hammond, gives you the Key to Snergle's Chambers which is needed in Castle Ironfist in the Snergle's Caverns . The door is locked and requires cell key from #1.\n3. Those cell doors open once you open the door at #2.\n4. Room with about 15 spell books.\nIn this dungeon are a lot of Dwarfs, so you need some good armor protection.\nThere are also a bunch of slime monsters, they are imune to physical damage, so use spells.\nOn the top floor is a room with about 15 spell books, but you will most likely already have those\nspells.","images":["MireOfTheDamned/snergles-iron-mines.gif"],"sourcePath":"MireOfTheDamned/snergles-iron-mines.html"},{"id":"mist-location","region":"Misty Islands","title":"Misty Islands","body":"Place : Mist\nA place with many islands.\n 1    Mist City [City Map]\n 2 Silver Helm Outpost [Map]\n 3 Teleporter, teleports to #4\n 4 Obelisk #14\n 5 Teleporter, teleports to #1\n 6 Throne Room with Lord Albert Newton\n 7 Fountain: +10 intellect and personality boost\n 8 Fountain: +5 elemental resistance boost\n 9 Shrine of Intellect [Shrine List] pray here in February\n 10 NPC: -2 days boat travel, +10% gold, -1 reputation category and takes 5% gold\n 11 Docks: Adventure [Travel Schedule]","images":["Mist/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"Mist/location.html"},{"id":"mist-city","region":"Misty Islands","title":"City Map","body":"Mist : City Map\n 1    Skills: Duelists' Edge ( trains in Mace, Bow, Chain, Shield and Bodybuilding )\n 2 Town Fire Tower\n 3 NPC: +8 points to disarm trap skill, -1 reputation category and costs nothing\n 4 Buccaneers' Lair Open: 6:00pm - 6:00am\n 5 Expert Leather Armor Training, Bucaneer's Lair Membership\n 6 Expert Repair\n 7 Expert Spear Training\n 8 Armor: Armor Emporium\n 9 Weapons: Arm's Length Spear Shop\n 10 Trainer: Island Testing Center only trains up to level 32\n 11 NPC: +5 perception, +10 luck and takes 4% gold\n 12 Expert: Staff Defense\n 13 Fountain: +20 Luck boost\n 14 Tavern: The Imp Slapper fills for 12 days\n 15 Fountain: +10 spell points regeneration\n 16 Temple: Mist Island Temple basic cost: 20 gold\n 17 Docks: Adventure [Travel Schedule]\n 18 Initiate Guild of Water\n 19 Initiate Guild of Air\n 20 Master Meditation\n 21 Bank: The Reserves\n 22 General Store: Lock, Stock, and Barrel\n 23 General Store: Witch's Brew\n 24 Master of Water\n 25 Master of Air\n 26 Master of Fire\n 27 Initiate Guild of Fire","images":["Mist/city.gif"],"sourcePath":"Mist/city.html"},{"id":"mist-silver-helm-outpost","region":"Misty Islands","title":"Silver Helm Outpost","body":"Mist : Silver Helm Outpost\nThis small post acts as an advance base for the Fraternal Order of Silver.\nFrom here, they are able to patrol Mist in their conquest of evil.\n 1    Prisoner, he tells about secret passage\n 2 Secret Door\n 3 Room with a switch, switch activates stairs in room next to it.\n 4 Stairs will come out of the wall, keep walking and you will reach the top of an elevator.\n 5 Melody Silver ( Damsel in Distress quest item :).\n 6 Stone picture will teleport you back down to the switch (#3.).\n 7 Gharik's Laboratory Key for Gharik's Forge\n 8 The switch on the wall will open the secret door to get into room at #7\nx - marks a spot where you can find a treasure chest or the likes\nLocal Enemies\nColor\nHP's\nType\nCaptain\n207\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nLieutenant\n93\nGuard\n45\nMaster Swordsman\n207\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nLieutenant\n93\nSwordsman\n40\nMaster Monk\n153\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nInitiate Monk\n73\nNovice Monk\n30","images":["Mist/silver-helm-outpost-pic.jpg","Mist/silver-helm-outpost-shot.jpg","Mist/silver-helm-outpost.gif"],"sourcePath":"Mist/silver-helm-outpost.html"},{"id":"newsorpigal-location","region":"New Sorpigal","title":"New Sorpigal","body":"Place : New Sorpigal\nYour party will start in this city, it has all the basic shops and people\nto get your party powerful enough to move into higher grounds.\n1. New Sorpigal [City Map]\n2. Abandoned Temple [Map]\n3. Ghariks Forge [Map]\n4. Goblinwatch [Map]\n5. Obelisk and 2x horseshoes\n6. NPC: Identification, takes 5% gold\n7. NPC: Cures party one a day, takes 5% gold\n8. Cook Pot, respawns enemies\n9. Expert Ancient Weapons\n10. Expert Water Magic\n11. Shrine of Luck [Shrine List] pray here in July\n12. Falagar the Gate Keeper - Your teacher from the game intro movie\n13. Expert Staff Defense\nLocal Enemies\nColor\nHP's\nType\nGoblin King\n40\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nGoblin Shaman\n21\nGoblin\n13\nMage\n207\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nJourneyman Mage\n21\nAprentis Mage\n6\nMaster Monk\n153\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nInitiate Monk\n73\nNovice Monk\n30","images":["NewSorpigal/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"NewSorpigal/location.html"},{"id":"newsorpigal-abandonedtemple","region":"New Sorpigal","title":"Abandoned Temple","body":"New Sorpigal : Abandoned Temple\nStrange squeaking echoes from behing the front doors. At one time\na temple of Baa, a foul curse caused the old inhabitants to move away.\n 1    The girl called Angela [Find Angela Quest]\n 2 A few Cobra Eggs, sells them in New Sorpigal\n 3 The Spider Queen [Kill Spider Queen Quest]\nLocal Enemies\nColor\nHP's\nType\nCobra\n17\nSnakes like the spiders are best dealt with from a distance. They can poison you when they strike.\nKing Cobra\n33\nQueen Cobra\n61\nBat\n9\nA few arrows should stop them before they even get close.\nGiant Bat\n30/td>\nVampire Bat\n35\nSpider\n17\nThese can be tough in the begining of the game. It's best to destroy them from a distance as they can poison you if they hit you.\nGiant Spider\n13\nQueen Spider\n50","images":["NewSorpigal/abandonedtemple-pic.jpg","NewSorpigal/abandonedtemple-shot.jpg","NewSorpigal/abandonedtemple.gif"],"sourcePath":"NewSorpigal/abandonedtemple.html"},{"id":"newsorpigal-city","region":"New Sorpigal","title":"City Map","body":"New Sorpigal : City Map\n1 Initiate Guild of Self\nExpert Learning Training (use back of building to get onto top floor)\n2 New Sorpigal Temple\n3 Initiate Guild of Elements\n4 Bridge to Abandoned Temple\n5 Expert: Earth Magic Training\n6 Expert: Fire Magic Training\n7 +5 spell points fountain (25 charges a day)\n8 +10 Might temporarily (5 charges a day?)\n9 Elemental Guild Membership, Quest to get spider queen heart\n10 Guild of Self Membership\nQuest to find Angela from Abandoned Temple\n11 Training Grounds\n12 Buccaneers' Lair ( trains in Merchant, Indentify, Perception and Disarm. Note that if you fly on the north ledge of the building and face south, you will be teleported to the Shrine of Gods if you press SPACE bar and search.)\n13 Town Hall\n14 The Common Defense\n15 Blades' End\n16 Expert Meditation Training\n17 Savings House with Expert of Air on top. Note that on the South side of the house you can find a Fly Scroll.\n18 +5 hit points fountain (30 charges a day)\n19 The Knife Shoppe\n20 The Seeing Eye\n21 Expert Body Building Training\n22 Expert Spirit Magic Training\n23 Expert Mind Magic Training\n24 Expert Body Magic\n25 Traveler's Supply\n26 Stables: Coach Company\n27 A Lonely Knight\n28 Buccaneers' Lair Membership, buys Cobra Eggs for 300 gold\n29 Blade's End Membership\n30 Main Gate to New Sorpigal, leads to Ironfist Castle (W), Goblinwatch (SW), Boat (E)","images":["NewSorpigal/city.gif"],"sourcePath":"NewSorpigal/city.html"},{"id":"newsorpigal-ghariks-forge","region":"New Sorpigal","title":"Gharik's Forge","body":"New Sorpigal : Gharik's Forge\nFire Elementals assisted Gharik in his attempts to create powerful items here. A handful of his powerfuls students continue his experiments.\nGharik's Forge\n1. Entrance\n2. There is a secret room here off to the side, and a switch to open the bridge\n3. This takes time. After Killing all the Fire Elementals, you have to make your way to each of the 4 doors, and hit the swithces to make the bridge move so that you can get across on the other side.\n4. Item the Hourglass of time from the [Find Hourglass Quest] .\n5. Letter to Marcus\n6. The key for this door is in Silver Helm Outpost\n7. There is about 10,000 gold down here, but there are a lof of the fire guy's down here.\nThis is a fairly tough one. You MUST have good fire protection and decent electrical protection if you plan on surviving for long at all.\nA person that is good with water magic is highly suggested, as they can do the most damage to the fire elementals with Ice Bold, or Ice Blast. The Magicians you'll just have to tough it out with.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["NewSorpigal/ghariks-forge-pic.jpg","NewSorpigal/ghariks-forge-shot.jpg","NewSorpigal/ghariks-forge.gif"],"sourcePath":"NewSorpigal/ghariks-forge.html"},{"id":"newsorpigal-goblinwatch","region":"New Sorpigal","title":"Goblinwatch","body":"New Sorpigal : Goblinwatch\nThe weathered stones of this old keep shelter empty buildings\nin an unused courtyard. Faint sounds echo from a worn stairway\nthat leads down below the keep.\nGoblinwatch\n1 Entrance\n2 Trapped Chest\n3 Trapped Chest with Goblin Code\n4 Chest\n5 Switch that allows access to 4\n6 Button Panel to open the doors at 7\nNILBOG or GOBLIN spelled backwards is one way to open the doors, there are others.\n7 Multiple Doors\n8 Alter Room, once this is cleared out, you can collect your money from Frank Fairchild in the New Sorpigal Town Hall\n9 Entrance to maintainance tunnels, you do not have to go down here.\nThere is not turning back once you fall.\n10 Four chest's in a room full of guy's, some Goblin Shaman's and Rat's\n11 Some gold on the beds\n12 Treasure Chest\n13 Treasure Chest\nLocal Enemies\nColor\nHP's\nType\nGiant Rat\n21\nThese guy's are weak, a few arrows should stop them before they get to you. If you are bitten, they can cause disease as well.\nLarge Rat\n13\nCommon Rat\n6\nSoul Sucker\n40\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nBrain Sucker\n13\nBlood Sucker\n6\nGoblin King\n40\nPretty much all magics work well against these guy's, there is no one that works best.\nGoblin Shaman\n21\nGoblin\n13","images":["NewSorpigal/goblinwatch-pic.jpg","NewSorpigal/goblinwatch-shot.jpg","NewSorpigal/goblinwatch.gif"],"sourcePath":"NewSorpigal/goblinwatch.html"},{"id":"paradisevalley-location","region":"Paradise Valley","title":"Paradise Valley","body":"Paradise Valley\nParadise Valley, that is not how I would describe it. Plenty of experience to be had and some nice items as well all the dragons leave something, the titans do as well and most of the Hydras.\nArea\nCity Map\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":[],"sourcePath":"ParadiseValley/location.html"},{"id":"paradisevalley-paradisevalley","region":"Paradise Valley","title":"City Map","body":"Paradise Valley: City Map\nParadise Valley\n1. Singing Steel\n2. The Last Chance (Inn)\n3. Sparring Ground\n4. Mighty Magicks\n5. The Enchated Hauberk\n6. Ancient Wepaons Master (an ancient weapon, and 5,000 gold)\n7. Dark Magic Master (notorius reputation)\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["ParadiseValley/Paradise.jpg"],"sourcePath":"ParadiseValley/ParadiseValley.html"},{"id":"paradisevalley-paradisevalley0","region":"Paradise Valley","title":"Surrounding area","body":"Paradise Valley: Surrounding area\n1. The City\n2. Obelisk\n3. Temple of Baa\n4. +100 power temporary.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["ParadiseValley/ParadiseValley.jpg"],"sourcePath":"ParadiseValley/ParadiseValley0.html"},{"id":"silvercove-location","region":"Silver Cove","title":"Silver Cove","body":"Place : Silver Cove\nA decent city, not as big as Free Haven, but you can buy things for less here, thanks to Abdul. This includes training.\n 1.  Silver Cove [City Map]\n 2. Warlords Fortress [Map]\n 3. Silver Helm Stronghold [Map]\n 4. The Monolith [Map]\n 5. Shrine of Personality [Shrine List] pray here in March\n 6. Oblisk #10\n 7. The Grove Inn\n 8. Ship Barracuda\n 9. A well that causes insanity, and increases Might Endurance, and speed, but decreases Intelligence and Endurance\n 10. Alter of the Sun [Quest]\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["SilverCove/land.gif"],"sourcePath":"SilverCove/location.html"},{"id":"silvercove-silvercove","region":"Silver Cove","title":"City Map","body":"Silver Cove : City Map\nSilver Cove\n 1.  Anchors Away Inn\n 2. Abdul's Discount Travel\n 3. Abdul's Discount Training Center\n 4. Well, +20 temporarily to Intellect, and Personality\n 5. Trader Joe's\n 6. Bank\n 7. Master Learning Training, 7 Skill and 30 Intellect\n 8. Berserker's Fury Membership 50 Gold\n 9. Master of the Mind (12 Skill, 4000 Gold) / Master of the Body (12 Skill, 4000 Gold)\n 10. Abdul's Discount Armor\n 11. Repair Expert 500 Gold\n 12. Berserker's Fury\n 13. Town Hall\n 14. Expert Light Magic 2000 Gold\n 15. Earth Guild Membership 100 Gold\n 16. Guild of Self Membership 100 Gold\n 17. Quest to Deface Monolith, Eleanor Vanderbilt\n 18. Expert Spear Training 2000 Gold\n 19. Abdul's Discount Weapons\n 20. Protection Services\n 21. Abdul's Discount Magic Supplies\n 22. Initiate Guild of Earth\n 23. Initiate Guild of Light\n 24. Master Earth Magic (12 Skill, 4000 Gold)\n 25. Expert Meditation 500 Gold\n 26. Adept Guild of Self\n 27. Master Merchant Training (10 Skill, 30 Intellect)\n 28. Silver Cove Temple\n 29. Quest to fix shipping prices,Castle Fliese\n 30. Quest to fix shipping prices,Castle Fliese\n 31. +2 to speed permanently\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["SilverCove/SilverCove.gif"],"sourcePath":"SilverCove/SilverCove.html"},{"id":"silvercove-silverhelm-stronghold","region":"Silver Cove","title":"Silverhelm Stronghold","body":"Silver Cove : Silverhelm Stronghold\nThe headquaters of the Fraternal Order of Silver and Sir John Silver's home.\nSilver Helms from this Stronghold patrol Silver Cove in search of evil.\nSilverhelm Stronghold\n 1.  Entrance\n 2. Lord Silverhelms Ghost\n 3. This is where you will find an Ankh. Take it to Loretta Fliese, and she will tell you to collect your reward from Lord Stone in White Cap .\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["SilverCove/silverhelm-stronghold-pic.jpg","SilverCove/silverhelm-stronghold-shot.jpg","SilverCove/silverhelm-stronghold.gif"],"sourcePath":"SilverCove/silverhelm-stronghold.html"},{"id":"silvercove-monolith","region":"Silver Cove","title":"The Monolith","body":"Silver Cove : The Monolith\nThis borboding structure radiates magical power. Druids from all over Enroth\nmake periodic pilgrimages to visit this sacred place.\nThe Monolith\n 1.  Entrance\n 2. Secret room. 5000 Gold in the little tree.\n 3. The main chamber. There is a letter in here that someone might want, and you have to deface the alter for the Quest Eleanor Vanderbilt.\nThis one is quite easy, there are no puzzles to it, an onlt the one hidden room which you would probably find anyway.\nThere are monsters from all the elemental magics except fire.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["SilverCove/monolith-pic.jpg","SilverCove/monolith-shot.jpg","SilverCove/monolith.gif"],"sourcePath":"SilverCove/monolith.html"},{"id":"silvercove-warlords-fortress","region":"Silver Cove","title":"Warlords Fortress","body":"Silver Cove : Warlords Fortress\nMuted sound of clashing metal and loud voices emanate from this imposing fortress.\nNo one would dare assult the Warlord's home.\nWarlords Fortress\n 1.  Entrance\n 2. The big door will NOT open, there is a secret one to the left of it, in there magical doors will warp you around a bit.\n 3. The Discharge Papers that Osric Temper wants as proof.\n 4. This is one of the may places to find large sums of money.\n 5. This is a hidden room with plenty of treasure, thanks to Godfather for pointing it out.\nThis one makes up for the easieness in the other two dungeons in Silver Cove. There are many veterans and soldiers here, but there are also Knights. Doom, Death, and Cuisinart Knights. They look very cool. Like Yoshimitsu in Tekken 3 for those of you who have played that.\nThe Cuisinart have close to or more than 1,000 hit points, so be prepared for a bit of a battle as they are never alone. I belive there were only five in the entire dungeon, but this seemd to occupy most of my time.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["SilverCove/warlords-fortress-pic.jpg","SilverCove/warlords-fortress-shot.jpg","SilverCove/warlords-fortress.gif"],"sourcePath":"SilverCove/warlords-fortress.html"},{"id":"sweetwater-location","region":"Sweet Water","title":"Sweet Water","body":"Place :Sweet Water\nNot much here anymore.\n1. The Hive [Map]\n2. Obelisk #1\n3. Pedestal\nPlace Statues [Quest] .\n4. +50 to all 7 stats temporarily.\nAll the oter fountains are poisonous.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["SweetWater/sweetwater.jpg"],"sourcePath":"SweetWater/location.html"},{"id":"sweetwater-hive","region":"Sweet Water","title":"The Hive","body":"Sweet Water : The Hive\n1. Entrance\n2. The switch to open up the central grate\n3. The Key to the reactor room\n4. The Reactor room entrance\n5. The Reactor\n6. The Queen, and the exit\nThere are a many demons in the large entry hall. If you can get past them the rest is pretty easy.\nDo not destroy the reactor if you don't have Dark containment, once you destroy it the walls fall down and you are warped in front of the queen. You should be able to run past her and into the small hallway. This will make you less of a target for all the others. Kill the Queen and then you can exit.\nNote: It has been found that a healer can heal you more than once per day in the hive. This is nice since you cannot cast Lloyd's beacon here and go get healed.\nYou have saved Enroth. Hope you had fun playing.\nLeave us a message mgrounds@hotmail.com\nThis Page was last updated on in the year of 1998.","images":["SweetWater/hive.jpg"],"sourcePath":"SweetWater/hive.html"}];
